# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate the time-evolution circuit {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "Validasi Circuit evolusi waktu {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you continue, compare the results with an independent implementation.\n"
"The `fermi_hubbard_1d` function of ffsim uses $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. This Hamiltonian equals the\n"
"Hamiltonian of this tutorial for $U' = U/2$ and $\\mu = U/4$, up to the constant $UL/8$. Therefore, the lowest eigenvalue at half filling must be the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum melanjutkan, bandingkan hasilnya dengan implementasi independen.\n"
"Fungsi `fermi_hubbard_1d` dari ffsim memakai $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. Hamiltonian ini sama dengan\n"
"Hamiltonian tutorial ini untuk $U' = U/2$ dan $\\mu = U/4$, hingga konstanta $UL/8$. Karena itu, nilai eigen terendah pada half filling harus sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same cell also checks the circuit itself. `FermionicCircuit` implements the `apply_unitary` protocol of ffsim, so ffsim can apply the\n"
"time-evolution circuit to a state vector directly. The code compares the result with the matrix exponential of the Hamiltonian, applied to\n"
"the same random state in the half-filling sector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sel yang sama juga memeriksa Circuit itu sendiri. `FermionicCircuit` mengimplementasikan protokol `apply_unitary` dari ffsim, sehingga ffsim bisa menerapkan\n"
"Circuit evolusi waktu ke state vector secara langsung. Kode membandingkan hasilnya dengan eksponensial matriks Hamiltonian, yang diterapkan ke\n"
"state acak yang sama pada sektor half-filling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encoding the fermions in qubits {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"
msgstr "3. Meng-encode fermion ke dalam qubit {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of spin ordering starts to matter when an encoding maps the modes to qubits, because the mode index then decides which qubits are neighbors.\n"
"To see this effect, use the same one-ancilla flow-set encoding that section 1 uses for the spinless case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pilihan urutan spin mulai berpengaruh saat encoding memetakan mode ke qubit, karena indeks mode kemudian menentukan qubit mana yang bertetangga.\n"
"Untuk melihat efek ini, pakai encoding flow-set satu-ancilla yang sama dengan yang dipakai bagian 1 untuk kasus tanpa spin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The effect appears as a Pauli pattern, which is a Pauli string together with the offsets of the qubits that it acts on. For example, `ZZ @ (0, 2)` is a Z on some qubit\n"
"$q$ and a Z on qubit $q+2$. The following table prints the patterns for each flow set. The patterns describe only the encoding register, not a\n"
"QPU. The layout decides how far apart two qubits are on a device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Efeknya muncul sebagai pola Pauli, yaitu string Pauli beserta offset qubit tempatnya bekerja. Misalnya, `ZZ @ (0, 2)` adalah Z pada suatu qubit\n"
"$q$ dan Z pada qubit $q+2$. Tabel berikut mencetak pola untuk setiap flow set. Pola ini hanya menggambarkan register encoding, bukan\n"
"QPU. Layout menentukan seberapa jauh dua qubit berada di sebuah perangkat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The east (`0`) and west (`1`) flow sets of the *blocked* ordering are the same as in the spinless case, because the hopping terms still act on nearest neighbors.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms, however, become weight-4 and scale with the length $L$ of the chain, as the pattern `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)` shows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Flow set timur (`0`) dan barat (`1`) pada urutan *blocked* sama seperti pada kasus tanpa spin, karena suku hopping tetap bekerja pada tetangga terdekat.\n"
"Namun, suku interaksi on-site menjadi berbobot 4 dan berskala dengan panjang $L$ rantai, seperti ditunjukkan pola `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, in the interleaved ordering, none of the encoded flow sets scale with the size of the system.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms remain weight-2 and are identical to the spinless case, because they act on nearest neighbors. The cost is more expensive hopping terms (`YY` and `ZXXZ`).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, pada urutan interleaved, tidak ada flow set terenkode yang berskala dengan ukuran sistem.\n"
"Suku interaksi on-site tetap berbobot 2 dan identik dengan kasus tanpa spin, karena bekerja pada tetangga terdekat. Harganya adalah suku hopping yang lebih mahal (`YY` dan `ZXXZ`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Pauli strings alone do not decide which ordering is cheaper in practice. The answer depends on\n"
"**which qubits the hardware can place next to each other**, and that connectivity is not necessarily one-dimensional.\n"
"A QPU can place the two chains of blocked order side by side, which a single line cannot do. Section 5 uses this property.\n"
msgstr ""
"String Pauli saja tidak menentukan urutan mana yang lebih murah dalam praktik. Jawabannya bergantung pada\n"
"**qubit mana yang bisa ditempatkan bersebelahan oleh hardware**, dan konektivitas itu belum tentu satu dimensi.\n"
"Sebuah QPU bisa menempatkan dua rantai urutan blocked berdampingan, yang tidak bisa dilakukan satu garis tunggal. Bagian 5 memakai properti ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"
msgstr "Transpilasi `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As shown previously, a single Trotter step is one `Evolution` gate that `FermionicLieTrotter` splits into one gate per flow set.\n"
"The `product_formula` argument of `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` then decides how each flow set becomes qubit gates.\n"
"This tutorial compares two synthesis paths:\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti ditunjukkan sebelumnya, satu langkah Trotter adalah satu Gate `Evolution` yang dipecah `FermionicLieTrotter` menjadi satu Gate per flow set.\n"
"Argumen `product_formula` pada `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` kemudian menentukan bagaimana setiap flow set menjadi Gate qubit.\n"
"Tutorial ini membandingkan dua jalur sintesis:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit `LieTrotter` synthesis, which synthesizes every Pauli rotation separately, in the order that it receives them.\n"
msgstr "Sintesis `LieTrotter` Qiskit, yang mensintesis setiap rotasi Pauli secara terpisah, dalam urutan penerimaannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A custom `FlowSetSynthesis` class (defined in the following cell) that uses the structure of the flow sets. It recognizes every Pauli shape that the\n"
"encodings in this tutorial produce (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, and, for two chains, the `ZZZZ` plaquettes), and\n"
"diagonalizes each flow set with a single Clifford layer. For these Hamiltonians, it does not need a term-by-term fallback,\n"
"and the code asserts that every term matches a known shape.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kelas `FlowSetSynthesis` kustom (didefinisikan di sel berikut) yang memanfaatkan struktur flow set. Kelas ini mengenali setiap bentuk Pauli yang dihasilkan\n"
"encoding dalam tutorial ini (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, dan, untuk dua rantai, plaket `ZZZZ`), dan\n"
"mendiagonalkan setiap flow set dengan satu layer Clifford. Untuk Hamiltonian ini, kelas ini tidak memerlukan fallback suku demi suku,\n"
"dan kode memastikan bahwa setiap suku cocok dengan bentuk yang dikenal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Work is in progress on an implementation that can find a low-depth diagonalizing Clifford circuit automatically.\n"
"Future releases of `qiskit-fermions` plan to support this feature, which can greatly simplify the use of flow-set-based fermion-to-qubit encodings.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"The following helper function constructs the transpiler pipeline and applies it to the `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"The function is useful in this tutorial because the flow-set encoding requires a `CustomF2QLayout`, which couples the transpiler pipeline to the fermionic circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sedang dikerjakan implementasi yang dapat menemukan Circuit Clifford pendiagonal berkedalaman rendah secara otomatis.\n"
"Rilis `qiskit-fermions` mendatang berencana mendukung fitur ini, yang dapat sangat menyederhanakan penggunaan encoding fermion-ke-qubit berbasis flow-set.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"Fungsi helper berikut membangun pipeline Transpiler dan menerapkannya ke `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"Fungsi ini berguna dalam tutorial ini karena encoding flow-set memerlukan `CustomF2QLayout`, yang menghubungkan pipeline Transpiler ke Circuit fermionik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Scaling of the interleaved mode ordering {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"
msgstr "4. Penskalaan urutan mode interleaved {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Start with the interleaved ordering and the encoding of section 3. With the one ancilla, there are $2L + 1$ qubits in a row. The\n"
"flow sets are `YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, and `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, and `FlowSetSynthesis` has a one-Clifford recipe for\n"
"each one. Build the circuit for $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, the size of every explicit check), and compare it with\n"
"`LieTrotter` before you measure anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mulai dengan urutan interleaved dan encoding dari bagian 3. Dengan satu ancilla, ada $2L + 1$ qubit dalam satu baris. Flow set-nya adalah\n"
"`YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, dan `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, dan `FlowSetSynthesis` punya resep satu-Clifford untuk\n"
"masing-masing. Bangun Circuit untuk $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, ukuran setiap pemeriksaan eksplisit), dan bandingkan dengan\n"
"`LieTrotter` sebelum kamu mengukur apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The previous check shows that the two circuits give identical results, up to a global phase.\n"
"The following drawing shows the regular structure that the flow-set encoding produces in the qubit circuit.\n"
"Later sections show how this structure helps you scale to larger systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemeriksaan sebelumnya menunjukkan bahwa kedua Circuit memberikan hasil yang identik, hingga fase global.\n"
"Gambar berikut menunjukkan struktur teratur yang dihasilkan encoding flow-set pada Circuit qubit.\n"
"Bagian selanjutnya menunjukkan bagaimana struktur ini membantu kamu melakukan penskalaan ke sistem yang lebih besar.\n"

