msgid ""
"The following drawing shows one of the routed circuits, for $L = 10$ on Heron (the best of the seeds, from the previous results).\n"
"Each wire is labeled `q_i ↦ p`, which means that virtual qubit `i` of the encoded circuit starts on physical qubit `p` of the device.\n"
"For Nighthawk, `p = 10 * row + col`. The drawing shows only the qubits that the circuit acts on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gambar berikut menunjukkan salah satu sirkuit hasil routing, untuk $L = 10$ di Heron (seed terbaik, dari hasil sebelumnya).\n"
"Setiap kabel diberi label `q_i ↦ p`, artinya qubit virtual `i` dari sirkuit yang dienkode dimulai di qubit fisik `p` pada perangkat.\n"
"Untuk Nighthawk, `p = 10 * row + col`. Gambar hanya menampilkan qubit yang dikenai operasi oleh sirkuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Connectivity of Nighthawk devices {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"
msgstr "5. Konektivitas perangkat Nighthawk {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The interleaved circuit needs only a path. Suppose the QPU offers more connectivity. The qubits of Nighthawk are on a square\n"
"lattice, and a square lattice contains a **ladder**: two parallel chains whose rungs are real couplers. A ladder is the\n"
"interaction graph of the Hubbard model in blocked order. The spin-up chain is on one rail, the spin-down chain is on the other, and the on-site term acts\n"
"across a rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sirkuit interleaved hanya butuh sebuah jalur. Misalkan QPU menawarkan konektivitas lebih. Qubit Nighthawk berada di kisi\n"
"persegi, dan kisi persegi memuat sebuah **tangga**: dua rantai paralel yang anak tangganya adalah coupler sungguhan. Tangga adalah\n"
"graf interaksi model Hubbard dalam urutan blocked. Rantai spin-up ada di satu sisi rel, rantai spin-down di sisi lainnya, dan suku on-site bekerja\n"
"melintasi anak tangga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The single-chain encoding of section 4 cannot use the ladder. It places all $2L$ modes along **one** chain. With blocked order,\n"
"the spin-up and spin-down blocks are joined end to end, and the on-site plaquettes stretch across the join. Instead, give\n"
"**each spin its own chain and its own ancilla**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengodean rantai tunggal di bagian 4 tidak bisa memakai tangga. Pengodean itu menaruh semua $2L$ mode sepanjang **satu** rantai. Dengan urutan blocked,\n"
"blok spin-up dan spin-down disambung ujung ke ujung, dan plakuet on-site membentang melintasi sambungan itu. Sebagai gantinya, beri\n"
"**setiap spin rantainya sendiri dan ancilla-nya sendiri**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-up modes $0..L-1$ are on qubits $0..L-1$, with the ancilla on qubit $L$.\n"
msgstr "Mode spin-up $0..L-1$ ada di qubit $0..L-1$, dengan ancilla di qubit $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-down modes $L..2L-1$ are on qubits $L+1..2L$, with the ancilla on qubit $2L+1$.\n"
msgstr "Mode spin-down $L..2L-1$ ada di qubit $L+1..2L$, dengan ancilla di qubit $2L+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each block uses the same images as before: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, and $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"where $q$ is the qubit of mode $j$. The total is $2L + 2$ qubits, which is one more than before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap blok memakai gambar yang sama seperti sebelumnya: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, dan $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"dengan $q$ adalah qubit dari mode $j$. Totalnya $2L + 2$ qubit, satu lebih banyak dari sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every flow set is now local on the ladder. The `X` and `ZXZ` terms act along a rail, and the interaction `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` is a 2x2\n"
"plaquette (two neighbors on one rail and the two qubits next to them on the other rail).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang setiap flow set bersifat lokal di tangga. Suku `X` dan `ZXZ` bekerja sepanjang rel, dan interaksi `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` adalah plakuet 2x2\n"
"(dua tetangga di satu rel dan dua qubit di sebelahnya di rel yang lain).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the encoded space, spin-up and spin-down operators now *commute* instead of anticommuting. This difference has no effect on this\n"
"Hamiltonian, because it contains only bilinears of the same spin and products of vertex operators. An operator with hopping between spins\n"
"raises an error in the action, so it cannot silently give a wrong answer. Perform the same check against\n"
"the known `LieTrotter` circuit as for the single-ancilla interleaved ordering:\n"
msgstr ""
"Di ruang yang dienkode, operator spin-up dan spin-down sekarang *komut* alih-alih antikomut. Perbedaan ini tidak berpengaruh pada\n"
"Hamiltonian ini, karena Hamiltonian-nya hanya berisi bilinear dari spin yang sama dan hasil kali operator vertex. Operator dengan hopping antar spin\n"
"akan memunculkan error pada aksinya, jadi tidak bisa diam-diam memberi jawaban yang salah. Lakukan pemeriksaan yang sama terhadap\n"
"sirkuit `LieTrotter` yang sudah dikenal seperti pada urutan interleaved dengan satu ancilla:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A ladder on the QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Tangga di QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A chain of $L + 1$ qubits fits on Nighthawk in a straight line if it has at most 12 qubits (along the 12 rows) or at most 10\n"
"(along the 10 columns). Therefore, up to $L = 11$, the two chains are side by side on two neighboring grid lines, rung by rung, and\n"
"every coupler that the circuit needs is a real coupler. The `folded_ladder` function returns this layout. For larger $L$, it also folds the ladder,\n"
"as section 6 describes. The function also selects the orientation that needs fewer strips, and selects the horizontal orientation if both need the same number.\n"
msgstr ""
"Rantai dengan $L + 1$ qubit muat di Nighthawk dalam garis lurus jika panjangnya paling banyak 12 qubit (sepanjang 12 baris) atau paling banyak 10\n"
"(sepanjang 10 kolom). Jadi, sampai $L = 11$, kedua rantai berdampingan di dua garis kisi yang bertetangga, anak tangga demi anak tangga, dan\n"
"setiap coupler yang dibutuhkan sirkuit adalah coupler sungguhan. Fungsi `folded_ladder` mengembalikan layout ini. Untuk $L$ yang lebih besar, fungsi ini juga melipat tangga,\n"
"seperti dijelaskan di bagian 6. Fungsi ini juga memilih orientasi yang butuh lebih sedikit strip, dan memilih orientasi horizontal jika keduanya butuh jumlah yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawings show both straight cases. For $L = 8$, a chain of 9 qubits fits along the 10 columns, so the ladder is\n"
"horizontal. For $L = 10$, a chain of 11 qubits does not fit along the 10 columns (it needs two strips), but it fits along\n"
"the 12 rows, so the layout uses a vertical ladder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gambar-gambar berikut menunjukkan kedua kasus lurus. Untuk $L = 8$, rantai 9 qubit muat sepanjang 10 kolom, jadi tangganya\n"
"horizontal. Untuk $L = 10$, rantai 11 qubit tidak muat sepanjang 10 kolom (butuh dua strip), tetapi muat sepanjang\n"
"12 baris, jadi layout memakai tangga vertikal.\n"

