# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Between $L = 10$ and $L = 12$, the depth of the blocked circuit increases from 10 to 25 in the `cz` basis (from eight to 23 with fractional\n"
"gates), and then stays the same up to $L = 50$. **The fold increases the depth once, not once per strip.** The drawing for $L = 50$ has four\n"
"folds and eight stretched links, and the depth is the same as at $L = 12$, which has one fold. The depth stays the same because the\n"
"depth penalties of all folds occur in parallel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Antara $L = 10$ dan $L = 12$, kedalaman sirkuit blocked naik dari 10 menjadi 25 di basis `cz` (dari delapan menjadi 23 dengan gerbang\n"
"fraksional), lalu tetap sama sampai $L = 50$. **Lipatan menaikkan kedalaman sekali saja, bukan sekali per strip.** Gambar untuk $L = 50$ punya empat\n"
"lipatan dan delapan tautan yang diregangkan, dan kedalamannya sama seperti pada $L = 12$, yang punya satu lipatan. Kedalamannya tetap sama karena\n"
"penalti kedalaman dari semua lipatan terjadi secara paralel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Result of the comparison.** Beyond the width of the QPU, blocked order loses its depth advantage. At $L = 50$, both orderings\n"
"reach 25 in the `cz` basis. The best interleaved seed reaches 22 between $L = 12$ and $L = 40$, but its median is 23 to 25.\n"
"With fractional gates, blocked order (23) is deeper than interleaved order (19). Blocked order still has a lower gate count: 462 compared with 838\n"
"in the `cz` basis (45% fewer) and 412 compared with 592 with fractional gates (30% fewer), at the cost of one more qubit. Fewer gates\n"
"can mean less accumulated error on a real device, which can be a reason to prefer blocked order on a QPU with a ladder. The\n"
"observable that you measure at the end of the circuit can also affect the choice of encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hasil perbandingan.** Melampaui lebar QPU, urutan blocked kehilangan keunggulan kedalamannya. Pada $L = 50$, kedua urutan\n"
"mencapai 25 di basis `cz`. Seed interleaved terbaik mencapai 22 antara $L = 12$ dan $L = 40$, tetapi mediannya 23 sampai 25.\n"
"Dengan gerbang fraksional, urutan blocked (23) lebih dalam daripada urutan interleaved (19). Urutan blocked tetap punya jumlah gerbang lebih rendah: 462 dibandingkan 838\n"
"di basis `cz` (45% lebih sedikit) dan 412 dibandingkan 592 dengan gerbang fraksional (30% lebih sedikit), dengan konsekuensi satu qubit tambahan. Gerbang yang lebih sedikit\n"
"bisa berarti error terakumulasi lebih sedikit di perangkat sungguhan, yang bisa jadi alasan untuk memilih urutan blocked di QPU dengan tangga.\n"
"Observable yang kamu ukur di akhir sirkuit juga bisa memengaruhi pilihan pengodean.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**On Heron, which has no ladder, blocked order is much worse.** Its best depth grows from 29 at $L = 4$ to 95 at $L = 50$\n"
"in the `cz` basis (92 with fractional gates), and the median and worst seeds at $L = 50$ give 134 and 166.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Di Heron, yang tidak punya tangga, urutan blocked jauh lebih buruk.** Kedalaman terbaiknya naik dari 29 pada $L = 4$ menjadi 95 pada $L = 50$\n"
"di basis `cz` (92 dengan gerbang fraksional), dan seed median dan terburuk pada $L = 50$ memberi 134 dan 166.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond one dimension {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"
msgstr "7. Melampaui satu dimensi {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of the previous sections are one-dimensional, where the hardware needs to hold only a path or a ladder. A square lattice of sites is\n"
"the case where the square connectivity of Nighthawk matters most, so this section briefly examines it. To keep the section short, it omits spin\n"
"and uses the **spinless** model of the [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard) guide\n"
"(Gandon et al., arXiv:2512.11418). That model has hopping and interaction on every nearest-neighbor bond of an $R \\times C$ lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semua bagian sebelumnya bersifat satu dimensi, di mana perangkat keras hanya perlu menampung sebuah jalur atau tangga. Kisi persegi dari situs adalah\n"
"kasus di mana konektivitas persegi Nighthawk paling berperan, jadi bagian ini membahasnya secara singkat. Agar bagian ini tetap ringkas, spin dihilangkan\n"
"dan dipakai model **spinless** dari panduan [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard)\n"
"(Gandon dkk., arXiv:2512.11418). Model itu punya hopping dan interaksi di setiap ikatan tetangga terdekat dari kisi $R \\times C$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Verstraete-Cirac encoding of the model, every site gets **its own ancilla** ($N = RC$ modes use $2N$ qubits), and the hopping splits into **four flow\n"
"sets** (east, west, north, and south). A Clifford circuit of two-qubit depth 2, which acts on all rows or all columns\n"
"at the same time, diagonalizes each flow set. As in 1D, the depth of the circuit therefore does not grow with the lattice. The guide shows each of these steps, but it\n"
"does not transpile to a given connectivity. The following drawing shows how the model fits on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada pengodean Verstraete-Cirac untuk model ini, setiap situs mendapat **ancilla-nya sendiri** ($N = RC$ mode memakai $2N$ qubit), dan hopping terpecah menjadi **empat flow\n"
"set** (timur, barat, utara, dan selatan). Sirkuit Clifford dengan kedalaman dua-qubit 2, yang bekerja pada semua baris atau semua kolom\n"
"sekaligus, mendiagonalkan setiap flow set. Seperti di 1D, kedalaman sirkuit karena itu tidak bertambah seiring kisi. Panduan tersebut menunjukkan setiap langkah ini, tetapi\n"
"tidak men-transpile ke konektivitas tertentu. Gambar berikut menunjukkan bagaimana model ini muat di Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The stripe layout on Nighthawk.** Lattice row $r$ runs down QPU column $r$ as a stripe that alternates site, ancilla, site,\n"
"ancilla (lattice column $c$ is on QPU rows $2c$ and $2c+1$). A site and its own ancilla are neighbors, an ancilla and the *next*\n"
"site along the row are neighbors, and vertical neighbors are on adjacent QPU columns. Therefore, **all hopping terms are on couplers**, and\n"
"the Clifford circuits need no routing. The interaction between two sites of the same row is not native, because the two sites are two QPU qubits\n"
"apart, with the ancilla between them (the red arcs). These pairs are the same $\\texttt{ZZ}$-type pairs that you routed in 1D, with one `rzz` gate per\n"
"horizontal bond, so the routing cost is similar to the cost in 1D. The largest lattice that fits this layout is $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 sites, which use all 120 qubits).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Layout strip di Nighthawk.** Baris kisi $r$ berjalan menyusuri kolom QPU $r$ sebagai strip yang bergantian situs, ancilla, situs,\n"
"ancilla (kolom kisi $c$ ada di baris QPU $2c$ dan $2c+1$). Sebuah situs dan ancilla-nya sendiri bertetangga, sebuah ancilla dan situs *berikutnya*\n"
"sepanjang baris bertetangga, dan tetangga vertikal ada di kolom QPU yang bersebelahan. Jadi, **semua suku hopping berada di coupler**, dan\n"
"sirkuit Clifford tidak butuh routing. Interaksi antara dua situs di baris yang sama tidak native, karena kedua situs itu terpisah dua qubit QPU\n"
"(dengan ancilla di antaranya, yaitu busur merah). Pasangan-pasangan ini adalah pasangan tipe $\\texttt{ZZ}$ yang sama seperti yang kamu routing di 1D, dengan satu gerbang `rzz` per\n"
"ikatan horizontal, jadi biaya routing-nya mirip dengan biaya di 1D. Kisi terbesar yang muat di layout ini adalah $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 situs, yang memakai semua 120 qubit).\n"

